WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:16.110
Unit eleven: Travel & Tourism News. Today you will give advice and warnings with first conditional and should / must.

4
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.028
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.478
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.387
Destination.

7
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:28.882
Destination means a place people travel to.

8
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:31.576
Angkor is a popular destination.

9
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:34.894
Your turn. Say: Destination.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.955
Destination.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.962
Travel advisory.

12
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.935
Travel advisory means an official warning about travelling to a place.

13
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.118
A travel advisory warned of heavy storms.

14
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:53.042
Your turn. Say: Travel advisory.

15
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.458
Travel advisory.

16
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.543
Tourism industry.

17
00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:04.233
Tourism industry means all the businesses that serve travellers.

18
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:07.571
The tourism industry creates many jobs.

19
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:10.929
Your turn. Say: Tourism industry.

20
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.035
Tourism industry.

21
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:17.075
Visa requirement.

22
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:22.126
Visa requirement means a rule about the permission needed to enter a country.

23
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:25.204
A new visa requirement began in March.

24
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:28.759
Your turn. Say: Visa requirement.

25
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.857
Visa requirement.

26
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:34.618
Peak season.

27
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:38.963
Peak season means the busiest time of year for tourists.

28
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.002
Hotels are expensive in peak season.

29
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:45.513
Your turn. Say: Peak season.

30
00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:49.449
Peak season.

31
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.451
Local economy.

32
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.727
Local economy means the money system of a town or region.

33
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:58.885
Tourists help the local economy.

34
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:02.159
Your turn. Say: Local economy.

35
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.257
Local economy.

36
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:08.587
Sustainable tourism.

37
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:13.824
Sustainable tourism means travel that does not harm nature or culture.

38
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:17.484
Sustainable tourism protects forests and villages.

39
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:21.107
Your turn. Say: Sustainable tourism.

40
00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:25.513
Sustainable tourism.

41
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.553
Cultural heritage.

42
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:32.837
Cultural heritage means traditions and historic places passed down over time.

43
00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.902
Cultural heritage attracts many visitors.

44
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:39.436
Your turn. Say: Cultural heritage.

45
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.626
Cultural heritage.

46
00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:47.922
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:48.783 --> 00:02:55.430
Visal, the news says 'If tourists ignore the travel advisory, they could face delays.' Which tense is that?

48
00:02:56.517 --> 00:03:06.019
It is the first conditional: if plus present simple, then will or could plus a base verb. It describes a real possibility.

49
00:03:07.117 --> 00:03:08.652
And the advice words?

50
00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:17.905
Should gives advice: visitors should check the visa requirement. Must gives a rule: tourists must respect the temple.

51
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:21.643
Why do travel articles use them so much?

52
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:28.871
Because they help readers prepare, and they protect both travellers and cultural heritage.

53
00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.557
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:32.417 --> 00:03:35.949
Grammar focus: First conditional with should and must.

55
00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.412
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.579
If tourists ignore the advisory, they could face long delays.

57
00:03:42.483 --> 00:03:44.808
Visitors should check the visa requirement.

58
00:03:45.717 --> 00:03:48.088
Tourists must respect the temple rules.

59
00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:55.993
If + present simple gives a real possibility. Do not use 'will' in the if-clause: say 'If it rains, flights will stop'.

60
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.180
Be careful! Don't say: If it will rain, flights stop.

61
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.864
Say: If it rains, flights will stop.

62
00:04:05.164 --> 00:04:06.641
No 'will' in the if-clause.

63
00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:10.631
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:12.469
Travel Smart.

65
00:04:12.769 --> 00:04:16.684
Tourism news helps travellers choose a destination and prepare for it.

66
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.254
If visitors arrive in peak season, they will pay more, so they should book early.

67
00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:28.947
A travel advisory or visa requirement can change quickly, and tourists must check it before they fly.

68
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:35.439
Sustainable tourism supports the local economy if travellers choose small, local businesses.

69
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:40.372
Respect for cultural heritage keeps a place beautiful for the future.

70
00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.352
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:46.217 --> 00:04:49.807
If tourists ignore the advisory, they blank face delays.

72
00:04:50.107 --> 00:04:53.377
A, could. B, would to. C, are.

73
00:04:56.933 --> 00:04:59.084
The answer is A: could.

74
00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.538
The busiest time of year for tourists is the blank season.

75
00:05:03.838 --> 00:05:06.992
A, peak. B, visa. C, quiet.

76
00:05:10.533 --> 00:05:12.138
The answer is A: peak.

77
00:05:13.283 --> 00:05:16.595
Travel that does not harm nature or culture is blank tourism.

78
00:05:16.895 --> 00:05:20.537
A, sustainable. B, local. C, advisory.

79
00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.459
The answer is A: sustainable.

80
00:05:27.617 --> 00:05:29.245
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:29.545 --> 00:05:35.787
A, If it will rain, we stay home.. B, If it rains, we will stay home.. C, If it rain, we stay home..

82
00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:42.285
The answer is B: If it rains, we will stay home..

83
00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.634
According to the reading, visitors should book early in…

84
00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:50.877
A, peak season. B, a storm. C, winter only.

85
00:05:54.433 --> 00:05:56.758
The answer is A: peak season.

86
00:05:57.967 --> 00:06:01.200
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.987
What responsibility do tourists have when visiting a place with fragile cultural heritage?

88
00:06:15.783 --> 00:06:17.156
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:17.456 --> 00:06:38.864
Tourists have a duty to protect it. They should follow the rules, avoid touching old walls or statues, and stay on the marked paths. If visitors behave carelessly, the heritage may be damaged forever. They should also support local guides, because that helps the community look after its history.

90
00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:40.989
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:41.883 --> 00:06:46.672
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and first conditional with should and must.

92
00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:52.271
Today's value is cultural respect. Learn from other cultures, and give credit to their people.

93
00:06:52.571 --> 00:06:55.270
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.246
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

